  "slug": "diana-microrna-cb45",
  "summary": "miRTarBase 11.0 and MIsoTEx add curated, tissue-resolved reference data for comparing regulatory relationships across tissues and experimental modalities.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the construction of structured reference resources that make regulatory evidence comparable across sources. miRTarBase 11.0 curates experimentally supported miRNA-target interactions and stresses that distinct experimental approaches capture distinct interaction types, so its evidence is organised around the assay behind each record. MIsoTEx extends this resource-building logic to transcript isoforms, classifying mammalian isoforms by tissue distribution, expression stability and abundance. The zebrafish ZebraMotif preprint takes a computational route, predicting transcription factor binding motifs for 2,543 TFs from AlphaFold3 and NA-MPNN protein-DNA structure models. The items differ in data type, so the shared element is the shift toward evidence-aware, tissue-resolved and structure-derived reference data.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
